// expect-error: T220
// Z3 corpus #47: axis-1 — Wall 4 Step 6 variant refinement violation.
//
// WHAT THIS FIXTURE PROVES
//
// The rejecting counterpart of fixture #46. The variant `Positive(x: i64)`
// declares `where x > 0`; the construction supplies `x: 0`. Z3 returns
// `Sat` for `not(0 > 0)`, so T220 fires at the construction site with
// the variant-qualified name `SignedInt::Positive`.
//
// Per V11 (inherited from Step 1), the dispatch maps Z3's `Sat` outcome
// to a T220 with the violated predicate and the supplied literal.
//
// Positive-literal comparison chosen to avoid SIGIL's binary-subtraction
// shape (`0 - 1`) which would be a `TypedExprKind::Binary` and fail
// V1's literal-only check with T211 rather than the intended T220.
//
// THE LANGUAGE PRIMITIVES THIS NEEDED
//
// Same as fixture #46 — this is the negative-evidence half of the pair.
// The verifier MUST reject; fixture #46 MUST accept.
//
// MUTATION CONTRACT
//
// Changing `0` to `5` (or any literal `> 0`) flips this fixture to
// the expect-ok side and drops T220. Removing the `where x > 0` clause
// weakens the contract entirely and drops T220.
module sigil;

enum SignedInt {
    Positive(x: i64) where x > 0,
    Zero,
    Negative(x: i64) where x < 0,
}

entry actor Main {
    on Tick() -> i64 {
        let p: SignedInt = Positive(0);  // MUTATION_SITE
        return 1;
    }
}
